  "query_preview": "..\n\nThe rest of today through Thursday..\n\nUpper level ridging will keep conditions warm and dry into next\nweek. Highs will increase from mostly 50s today to 60s to low 70s\nby Sunday. A weak shortwave Monday into Tuesday will knock highs\nback into 50s, increase clouds, and may allow for an isolated \nshower over the mountains (<20% chance). Highs then increase into\nthe 60s to near 70 for midweek as the ridge builds in again.\n\nWinds will be strong at times over the western foothills today\ninto Sunday, with gusts generally around 30 to 45 mph. These\nstrong crosswinds may impact travel along Interstate 90 from Big\nTimber through Livingston and Highway 191 from Big Timber to \nHarlowton. Gap winds are favored for Livingston tonight and \nSaturday night under a favorable pressure gradient. 700 mb winds \nare expected to increase to around 30 to 40 kts out of the west \ntonight, which is not the most favorable direction for strong gap \nwinds. Then, 700 mb winds turn out of the southwest (favorable for\nstrong gap winds) and increase to 45 to 55 kts Saturday night. \nCurrently for Livingston, there is a 40% chance of a wind gust \ngreater than 50 mph tonight and a 70% chance Saturday night. Across\nthe rest of the region, winds will be occasionally breezy, with \ngusts into the 20s mph. Archer",
